Subject: [PATCH] econet-eth: accept EN751627 special-tag sport values

With the GDM1 special tag (STAG) enabled for the DSA conduit, EN751627
reports 8 + switch port in the RX descriptor sport field (lan1 = 11,
wan = 12, ...). The switch port itself is carried by the DSA tag, so
treat every value with bit 3 set as GDM1 and only report other
unexpected values, rate-limited.

--- a/econet_eth.c
+++ b/econet_eth.c
@@ -148,8 +148,10 @@ static struct net_device *en75_get_sport_dev(struct en75_eth_pvt *eth,
 	if (sport == ETX_FPORT_GDM2) {
 		return eth->ports[1];
 	} else {
-		if (sport != ETX_FPORT_GDM1)
-			dev_info(eth->pub.dev, "rx: on unexpected fport %d\n", sport);
+		if (sport != ETX_FPORT_GDM1 && !(sport & BIT(3)))
+			dev_info_ratelimited(eth->pub.dev,
+					     "rx: on unexpected fport %d\n",
+					     sport);
 		return eth->ports[0];
 	}
 }
